
  <sn><md>### PCBs — Polychlorinated Biphenyls

**PCBs (Polychlorinated Biphenyls)** are a group of **synthetic organic chemicals** consisting of two benzene rings with varying numbers of chlorine atoms attached to them.

They are classified as **persistent organic pollutants (POPs)** because they are highly persistent in the environment and can accumulate in living organisms.


Basic structure

A PCB molecule contains:

```text
        Cl
         |
   C₆H₄ — C₆H₄
      |       |
     Cl      Cl
```

The two benzene rings are joined together, and **1–10 chlorine atoms** can replace hydrogen atoms on the rings.

There are **209 possible PCB congeners**, differing in the number and position of chlorine atoms.
</md></sn>
